r forming Chows in Bamboos. Therefore, the answer is Play T6.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Discard T6 to preserve potential for forming Chows in Bamboos and Characters, while reducing terminals which hinder high-scoring patterns like All Chows or Fully Concealed Hand.  \nReason: T6 is a terminal tile in Bamboo, not part of any current or potential Chows. Discarding it retains B1/B2 (for B1-2-3 Chow) and T3/T4 (for T3-4-5 Chow if T5 is drawn), which are more valuable for forming Chows. Keeping W1-2-3 (Chow) and W5-6-6 (potential Pung or Chow with W4/W7) also strengthens hand flexibility.  \nAnswer: Play T6"}
